ForeverCompanionData.news = {
  {id="0.4.2",d="2026-10-20",t="# New\n- **Auction House**: the price graph now also shows how many of the item were on sale each day (blue line, scale on the right). Hover the graph to see the price and the number on sale for each day.\n- Click **lowest buyout** or **number on sale** above the graph to hide or show that line. Your choice is kept."},
  {id="0.4.1",d="2026-10-16",t="# Improvements\n- **Items on my characters**: item tooltips now show the 3 characters who have the most of an item, starting with the one you are playing. Hold **Alt** to see them all. Choose how many in Options > Items & loot.\n- Faction filter is now complete and looks functionnal, please tell me on **CurseForge** if anything looks wrong.\n\n# Fixes\n- Fixed an error that could appear in combat if you had the nodes on your map. It's now fixed and you can keep using nodes without any new error."},
  {id="0.4.0",d="2026-10-12",t="**TEMPORARY FIX**\n\n# NEW : Quick setup\n- New check mark button at the top of the BiS window: turn each feature on or off in one click (herbs and ore on the maps, item scores, trainer spells, Auction House, minimap button...).\n- Your detailed settings are kept for when you turn a feature back on. More settings are in Options > Tabs & features.\n\n# NEW : Trainer spells\n- A new list next to your spellbook: open it with P, then click the tab on its edge. It shows every spell your class trainer teaches, with its level and price.\n- The number on the tab tells how many spells you can learn now.\n- Warlocks also see the grimoires of the demon trainer.\n\n# NEW : Items on my characters\n- Item tooltips show how many each character of your realm has: bags, equipment, bank, mail and auctions.\n- In Options > Items & loot, choose whether to include the characters of the other faction, or forget a deleted character.\n\n# Factions\n- Items of the other faction are detected much more reliably: quest rewards, reputation items (League of Arathor, Stormpike, Frostwolf...) and PvP items. Description can be wrongfully saying horde or alliance, don't mind it, it'll we fixed.\n- Class quest rewards that both factions can get on Forever are no longer hidden.\n- Item tooltips now show the rank of the item in the BiS lists of your faction, like the BiS window.\n- The faction emblem next to the Phase menu shows the BiS list of the other faction.\n\n# Gathering\n- Herbs and ore now show only on the world map by default; turn the minimap on in Quick setup.\n- Their icons are smaller by default, and you can choose their size in Options > Professions.\n\n# Other changes\n- Right-click a side tab of the BiS window to open its options.\n- Fixed a small freeze when leveling up.\n\nThank you all for your feedback."},
  {id="0.3.0",d="2026-10-09",t="# New: Guided tour\n- Click the **?** button of the BiS window for a step-by-step tour of the windows and options (also in Options > About, or type /fc tour).\n\n# New: Tabs & features\n- One page to choose what the addon shows: hide the tabs you don't use, or turn off **Gathering locations** and **Gear scales** in one click. Your settings are kept.\n\n\n# New: Faction filter\n- Quest rewards, PvP and reputation items of the other faction are hidden from the BiS list and Dungeon Loot (Options > Items & loot). If you still see some items that i might have missed please tell me in the addon comments on Curse Forge.\n\n**Improvements**\n- This window opens once after each update\n- Gathering: better zone recognition, no more nodes inside capital cities.\n\n\nThank you all so much for the support, I hope you have a wonderfull time in WoW Forever!"},
  {id="0.2.4",d="2026-10-07",t="**New: Gear scales**\n\n- Every item now shows a score in its tooltip, based on stat weights for your class and spec, compared to what you're wearing. (Scales will be changed some of them are unbalanced atm)\n- Green arrow on quest rewards and loot rolls when an item is an upgrade.\n- Gold star for your best-in-slot item, grey star for alternatives from your BiS list.\n- Scale picked automatically from your talents, or choose your own. Copy and edit any scale, and import or export scales as text to share them.\n\n**New: Gathering nodes**\n\n- Herbs and ore veins shown on the world map and the minimap.\n- Icons turn into a colored ring when you're close, so you can still see the game's tracking dot.\n- Nodes you gather yourself are added to your map.\n- Key bindings to show or hide the icons on each map, set right in the addon options.\n\n**New: Crafting profit**\n\n- The professions window can show the profit of each recipe, using Auction House and vendor prices.\n\n**Improvements & fixes**\n\n- All WoW Forever zones should now be recognized, including the new ones."},
}
